Subject: wifi: ath11k: pair NSS init rejection and descriptor ownership

Unwind the SoC registration when the existing state check rejects NSS
initialization. Preserve the original admission point: NSS may become ready
during descriptor allocation, so rejecting it earlier can regress startup.
The unregister API also returns an external interface reservation.

Use the coherent allocation's CPU pointer as the ownership predicate and
clear all descriptor metadata after release. This also preserves a valid
DMA address of zero. NULL calls were already guarded by the Linux DMA
wrapper; this is not a claim of a reproduced low-level double free.

These changes do not establish firmware quiescence or callback draining
after a command timeout. The shared completion and final teardown contract
still require a joint lifecycle repair; do not force-free those resources.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -4156,10 +4156,10 @@ static void ath11k_nss_tx_desc_mem_free(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	for (i = 0; i < ATH11K_NSS_MAX_NUMBER_OF_PAGE; i++) {
-		if (!ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i])
-			continue;
-
-		dma_free_coherent(ab->dev,
-				  ab->nss.tx_desc_size[i],
-				  ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i],
-				  ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i]);
+		if (ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i])
+			dma_free_coherent(ab->dev,
+					  ab->nss.tx_desc_size[i],
+					  ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i],
+					  ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i]);
 		ab->nss.tx_desc_vaddr[i] = NULL;
+		ab->nss.tx_desc_paddr[i] = 0;
+		ab->nss.tx_desc_size[i] = 0;
 	}
@@ -4527,6 +4527,6 @@ static int ath11k_nss_init(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	if (nss_cmn_get_state(nss_contex) != NSS_STATE_INITIALIZED) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "nss state in default init state\n");
-		goto free;
+		goto unregister;
 	}
 
